ts><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KINOMURA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KINOMURA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KINOMURA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KINOMURA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>When a load of an antenna changes instantaneously, a cellular phone detects the load change in real time and compensates for it. The characteristic curves of power efficiency and gain of a power amplifier are drawn together on a Smith chart beforehead. The range of the operating points of the amplifier is estimated on the Smith chart from the results of measurements of the current and gain of the amplifier. The direction and level of the change in the input impedance of the amplifier is determined using impedance information contained in the Smith chart. The change is compensated for by controlling a variable-load circuit.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Lorsqu'une charge d'une antenne se modifie instantanément, un téléphone cellulaire détecte cette modification de charge en temps réel et la compense. Les courbes caractéristiques du rendement énergétique et du gain d'un amplificateur de puissance sont préétablies en même temps sur un abaque de Smith. La plage des points de fonctionnement de l'amplificateur est évaluée sur l'abaque de Smith à partir des mesures obtenues de courant et de gain de l'amplificateur. La direction et le niveau de modification de l'impédance d'entrée de l'amplificateur sont déterminés par des informations d'impédance contenues dans l'abaque de Smith. La modification est compensée par la commande d'un circuit à charge variable.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>